nsequences just  because of what we saw in the video and  just because of their other rhetoric  um i assume that it will have an impact  i also suspect though that  they may suddenly decide they want to  plead to the feds rather than face  another lifestyle  right right and we're already hearing  that uh there's going to be an appeal as  well potentially i also sticking with  federal responses want to talk about  president biden's reaction uh in in  response to the written house verdict he  said the jury system works and we have  to abide by it  what did you make of that reaction and  i'm curious also if you could  tell me what grade you would give the  white house's response to these trials  that we've seen over the course of the  past couple weeks  uh is it  is there something below an f like what  are we doing is there a z grade for this  because  while i understand that he is the  president and this is sort of what the  speech writers have come up with and  this is where you know governing the  entire country  um the jury system didn't really work in  the red house trial in my opinion okay  granted we do really love the idea of  the jury system working  but if you can recognize that what the  jury did here wasn't enough and not  enough has occurred you probably should  have been able to recognize that what  happened with written house was also not  enough  yeah thank you for explaining that um in  our final minute together mickey i'm  curious if there's anything else that  you are looking ahead  to uh in terms of what this verdict  could mean not just for the black  community but again for the country as a  whole i know you mentioned that this  isn't something to be  optimistic about in your view um  how do you think it affects our country  going forward then  i think unless our country is willing to  admit that this was a lynching and that  it took a lynching on video for them to  even consider a conviction  we're not really moving that fast  america spent more time with lynching  being legal than uh we ever want to  admit  and we are still to some degree saying  well yes okay this time we're gonna  we're gonna hold this person accountable  but we're not gonna hold the system that  made them think committing a lynching  was acceptable accountable we're not  going to look at the people who would  have enabled them to get away with it if  they could  we're just going to say this time the  lynching didn't happen see progress i  would like us to not get to a point  where we have to see a video of someone  being murdered in cold blood before we  acknowledge that they probably shouldn't  have been killed for running  absolutely mickey really appreciate you  joining us and giving us all of your  analysis and thoughts on this verdict  thank you so much and again i'll remind  our audience that was mickey kendall  she's an author and diversity consultant  as
 

